    "q-81396": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81396",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=5.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-5B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5=5A\\,⟹\\,A=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81396-a",
